{
 "name": "sword_cut_j4",
 "note": "TRIAL (2026-11-18), the everyday cut from the accepted stance stand_sword_j6 and back to it (fourth take). From the wind (old t130) to the end of the follow (old t440) it is sword_cut exactly, 20 ms later. Start: no sink; the body rises out of the lunge and rears back straight into the wind (one fast-start ease, like the kept cut), the sword rising clockwise behind the back, the feet gathered in two quick overlapping lifted steps. Return: a recoil on planted feet with the arm out front and the blade in line, a bound back home (travel only while both feet are up) with the sword arm lagging out in front, the point at the enemy, to the top of the jump; then one whip down and back under the shoulder, the hand leading and the blade dragging until the grip is behind the hips, the blade flipping up behind the rear leg as he lands, a little past its rest in the sink, then the stance (the last frame is stand_sword_j6@0). Made by art/redo/stand/mktrial_j.py.",
